 "text": "Hi, how's everything with you? Try starting with simple line drawing, and only a few details at first. Eyes are tiny and often at first they look scared or puffed. Rough as little drawings with few lines. Then, once the basics of the face are there, add the eyeballs. Start it with just one line, and then copy it several times. Then, for each copy, try changing something. The eyeball position always surprises me. Enjoying the process rather than result makes drawing so much more enjoyable.",
